#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
WORK="${FIRST_TOUCH_WORK:-$(mktemp -d /tmp/forgeops-first-touch-ai.XXXXXX)}"

cat <<'INTRO'
ForgeOps with a real model

Give AI the ability to operate -- not unrestricted authority over the
environment.

A real model sits in the requester seat. It gets the tools and nothing else: no
shell, no credential, no route, and no way to approve its own request. It reads
the connector, works out what is wrong, and asks for an operation. What happens
to that request is the demo.

The model runs on our side. Nothing about your machine is sent to it except
what you type and what the demo's own connector reports, and you can point this
at your own endpoint instead -- see the README.
INTRO

# The hosted relay holds the model credential so you need none. Override it
# with your own endpoint and key if you would rather nothing left this machine
# for ours; the demo is identical either way.
FORGE_MODEL_ENDPOINT="${FORGE_MODEL_ENDPOINT:-https://relay.forgeops.ykdynamics.com}" \
FIRST_TOUCH_BIN_DIR="$HERE/bin" \
FIRST_TOUCH_METADATA="$HERE/metadata.env" \
FIRST_TOUCH_WORK="$WORK" \
FIRST_TOUCH_COMMANDS_BEFORE_READY=1 \
FIRST_TOUCH_CHAT=1 \
bash "$HERE/scripts/first-touch-local.sh"
